    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Overview</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Aquarium at August 32nd is a short walking simulator game inspired by the well-known horror simulator Exit 8. In this game, players explore a spooky aquarium filled with anomalies and must find a way to exit by identifying these differences.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The rule of Aquarium at August 32nd is simple: turn back if there is an anomaly, or go forward if there is none. The game is completed when the number of jellyfish in the tank reaches eight.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play time: 15 to 60 minutes</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Video Distribution Guidelines</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both individuals and corporations can distribute without permission.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Monetization is possible only when using the functions provided by the video distribution site.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We will not be liable for any damages whatsoever resulting from the distribution of videos of this game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The contents of these guidelines are subject to change without notice.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Mouse &amp; Keyboard]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Move: W, A, S, D keys</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Run: Shift key</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Camera control: Mouse movement</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Gamepad]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Move: L stick</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Run: Press L stick or L trigger </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Camera control: R stick</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Option Setting</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the options menu, the following settings are available</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Language: \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e / English</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >window mode: full screen / window</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Frame Rate Upper Limit: Adjustable up to 60</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Volume: Adjustable from 0.0 to 1.0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Camera Sensitivity: Adjustable from 0.0 to 1.0</p>",
